A||||2||Fierodave2001||News on latest car show||||6||
Z||000000||Fierodave2001||04-23-2001||10:47 AM||||Hello to all,   <BR> <BR>There was another car show held in Punta Gorda, Fl this past weekend (4-21 & 4-22). This was an open show to all types & makes.<BR> <BR>This was 27th Annual Automobile Festival Show, Peace River Region -AACA-.<BR> <BR>I've been going to this show since 1989, and was the only Fiero entered that year.  I won <BR>1st place in the class which was called late <BR>model production & kit cars.  That was a  large class, ranging from 1976 - present all car types.  There were quite a few in that class.<BR> <BR>In 1999 & 2000 there were 2 Fieros entered, (same class). My car took 2nd in both!<BR> <BR>Now this year, 2001, there were 5 Fieros entered !!  Quite a few Fiero owners came  over and said they might bring their cars next year. The judges put us in a strange  class, call imports & sport cars. Along with  the "Rice burners" there was a "007" style 1959 "gullwing" Mercedes, silver in mint condition. It even had the original  luggage and tools that came with the car.  The tools to remove the knock off spinner wheels. It was a 110 point out of 100 car.  <BR> <BR>- Anyway back to Fiero's,  The judges said it was really close, and gave 1st place to  the Mercedes, I took 2nd, and another Fiero  owned by Paul Ignozza took third. His was an  87 wingless GT V6, repainted in Blue.<BR> <BR>Next year the judges told me they were going  to create a class that would put the Fiero's in a class, not competing with imports. -As it should be.<BR> <BR>I'll keep all posted for next years show  when they announce the date, maybe we could  have more Fieros come, and show those Rice burners whose really boss !<BR> <P>And yes, mine's the Blue 87GT one that won Best of Show in the Daytona 2001 show. (not  bragging, well, maybe a little)<BR> <BR>(I'm still so proud and honored to have it chosen to represent all the cars that were there this year.) Fieros rule !<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Fierodave2001 (edited 04-23-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000001||Old Lar||04-23-2001||11:38 AM||||Bragging rights are yours because you have the car.  Congratulations.||||reg||10
Z||000002||Fierodave2001||04-23-2001||11:08 PM||||Thanks OLD LAR. Good to hear from U.<P>I'm glad to see more and more Fiero's being entered in these open shows.  <P>It was funny, when the T-bird owners set up their cars, they promptly started to put up a tent in front of our Fieros.  I asked them to please select another site.  They got real nasty, and bitched to rest of the day. <P>They were surprized over the crowd we were drawing away from their Thunderbirds. Ha, I loved it.<P>We choose a great location with the river as a back drop to put our Fieros.  <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/PG1_1.jpg"> <p>[This message has been edited by Fierodave2001 (edited 04-23-2001).]||||reg||14
